  "aiContextParagraph": "The Brazilian government has publicly opposed recent proposals from the United States regarding new tariffs on specific Brazilian products, including aircraft and sugar. Government representatives, including the Vice President, have described the proposed levies as unreasonable and suggested they could ultimately prove detrimental to the American market itself. Official statements from Brazil indicate a firm stance against the trade pressure, with authorities declaring they will not yield to threats. Meanwhile, stakeholders such as the American Chamber of Commerce in Brazil are preparing to participate in formal US consultation processes to address the matter. Analysts and political observers are currently debating whether the current administration can successfully negotiate with the US government to de-escalate the trade friction. The affected exports, which represent approximately 7 percent of Brazil's total trade with the US, remain a focal point of these ongoing diplomatic and economic discussions.",
